# Local Deployment

## Architecture
Server, worker, and frontend run natively (not in Docker). Postgres, Redis, MailHog in Docker.

## Ports
| Service | Port |
|---|---|
| Server (FastAPI) | 8000 |
| Frontend (Next.js) | 3000 |
| Postgres (main) | 5434 |
| Postgres (unit test) | 5435 + 5438–5440 |
| Postgres (integration test) | 5436 |
| Postgres (e2e test) | 5437 |
| Redis | 6379 |
| MailHog (email catch-all) | 8025 |
| Adminer (DB browser) | 8081 |

## Config
- `local.env` — git-tracked, non-secrets (service URLs, feature flags, dev settings).
- `.env` — git-ignored, secrets only (`DQT_CREDS_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, DB passwords).

## First-time setup
```bash
make install               # uv sync + pnpm install
./run_local/start.sh       # Docker stack up + migrations + demo seed
make dev-server            # FastAPI on :8000 (hot reload via uvicorn --reload)
make dev-web               # Next.js on :3000 (hot reload)
```

## Daily dev
```bash
make dev-server            # FastAPI on :8000
make dev-web               # Next.js on :3000
# Worker (if needed):
make dev-worker            # arq worker
```

Hot reload: frontend and backend reload automatically — don't restart them.

## Server modes
- `uvicorn dqt_server.main:app --reload` — dev (hot reload, debug logging)
- `./run_local/start-server-prod.sh` — Gunicorn + uvicorn workers (production-like)

## Demo seed data
```bash
dqt demo seed
```
Populates the local Postgres with:
- 1 tenant + 1 admin user (`admin@dqt.local` / `password`)
- 1 Postgres source (pointing at synthetic `analytics` schema in same DB)
- 3 datasets: `fct_orders`, `fct_sessions`, `dim_customers`
- ~20 checks (mix of rule-based and statistical)
- Pre-run check history with injected anomalies
- 3 open incidents (so Overview and Incidents aren't empty on first load)

## Docker stack (`run_local/docker-compose.yml`)
| Service | Image | Port |
|---|---|---|
| postgres | `postgres:16` | 5434 |
| redis | `redis:7-alpine` | 6379 |
| mailhog | `mailhog/mailhog` | 8025 |
| adminer | `adminer` | 8081 |

## Migrations
```bash
make db-migrate            # alembic upgrade head
make db-rollback           # alembic downgrade -1
```

## Validate the stack
```bash
make test-lib              # library tests (<60s)
make lint                  # ruff + mypy + eslint + tsc
open http://localhost:3000  # UI should show demo data
```
